      ":question/problem": "![](images/d6/d6cfde66c20829ea57cb94d46e231fb3c2ec1099610e4f052bc90a725bf285db.png)\n\nIn a track and field event, two heats of athletes participated in a long jump contest. The median jump distance in Heat A was $8.1$ meters. The histogram above shows the jump distances for Heat B.\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe median jump distance in Heat B lies in the group\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe median jump distance in Heat B is\n{{field-2}}\nthe median jump distance in Heat A.\n\nBased on the median values,\n{{field-3}}\nhad athletes jumping farther on average."
